invariant: INV-48
file: keccak_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-avx2
reason: the four-way round rotates lane 6 by 43 where FIPS 202's rho
  rotates it by 44, so every stream differs from sha3.c's after the
  first round. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds
  bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    lanes b1 = lanes_rotate_left(a[6], 44);
--- new
    lanes b1 = lanes_rotate_left(a[6], 43);
